%N A398693 Cardinality of the unique largest subdirectly irreducible factor of the lattice of partitions of n under the dominance order.
%C A398693 The set of partitions of n can be given a complete lattice structure as first shown by Brylawski. This lattice has an irredundant decomposition as a subdirect product of subdirectly irreducible factor lattices; for n >= 13, there is a unique largest factor lattice in this decomposition, the size of which is a(n). For n < 13 the subdirectly irreducible factors of highest cardinality are not always unique and have a different structure not fitting the size formula conjectured to hold below.
%C A398693 The values a(n) for 13 <= n <= 60 were derived using methods of Formal Concept Analysis by exploiting the fact that a(n) is also the size of the concept lattice of the largest one-generated arrow-closed subcontext of the standard context of Brylawski's integer partition lattice.
%H A398693 A. Almazaydeh, M. Behrisch, E. Vargas-García and A. Wachtel, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijar.2024.109244">Arrow relations in lattices of integer partitions</a>, Internat. J. Approx. Reason., 172 (2024), paper 109244, pp. 1-24.
%H A398693 M. Behrisch, E. Vargas-García and A. Wachtel, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijar.2026.109726">Lattices of integer partitions are almost subdirectly indecomposable</a>, Internat. J. Approx. Reason., 197 (2026), paper 109726, pp. 1-23 (includes terms of this sequence for 13 <= n <= 32 and n=42, see p. 21 et seq.).
%H A398693 M. Behrisch, E. Vargas-García and A. Wachtel, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18895342">Standard contexts and arrow-closed subcontexts of integer partition lattices</a>.
%H A398693 T. Brylawski, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/0012-365X(73)90094-0">The lattice of integer partitions</a>, Discrete Math., 6(3) (1973), 201-219.
%H A398693 B. Ganter, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijar.2021.11.004">Notes on integer partitions</a>, Internat. J. Approx. Reason., 142 (2022), 31-40.
%H A398693 B. Ganter and R. Wille, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-63422-2">Formal Concept Analysis. Mathematical foundations</a>, 2nd Edition, Springer, Cham, 2024, pp. xii+370.
%F A398693 Conjecture: a(n) = A000041(n) - 4*n + 7 - (-1)^n (verified for n <= 60).
%Y A398693 Cf. A000041.
